        "answer": "",
        "alternateAnswers": [],
        "explanation": "The given quadratic equation is $x^2 - 5x - 14 = 0$. We can solve this by factorization: Find two numbers that multiply to -14 and add to -5. These numbers are -7 and 2. So, $x^2 - 7x + 2x - 14 = 0$ $x(x - 7) + 2(x - 7) = 0$ $(x - 7)(x + 2) = 0$ Therefore, $x - 7 = 0$ or $x + 2 = 0$. $x = 7$ or $x = -2$. The roots are 7 and -2.",
