            "isCorrect": false,
            "index": 3,
            "imageUrl": "",
            "explanation": ""
          }
        ],
        "answer": "",
        "alternateAnswers": [],
        "explanation": "Let the first term be 'a' and the common difference be 'd'.\nGiven:\nT₅ = a + 4d = 18  --- (1)\nT₁₁ = a + 10d = 36 --- (2)\n\nSubtract (1) from (2):\n(a + 10d) - (a + 4d) = 36 - 18\n6d = 18\nd = 3\n\nSubstitute d = 3 into (1):\na + 4(3) = 18\na + 12 = 18\na = 6\n\nNow, find the sum of the first 10 terms (S₁₀):\nSₙ = n/2 * [2a + (n-1)d]\nS₁₀ = 10/2 * [2(6) + (10-1)3]\nS₁₀ = 5 * [12 + 9(3)]\nS₁₀ = 5 * [12 + 27]\nS₁₀ = 5 * 39\nS₁₀ = 195",
