        "explanation": "Let the roots of the quadratic equation px² + qx + r = 0 be α and β.\nGiven that α : β = 2 : 3.\nLet α = 2k and β = 3k for some constant k.\n\nFrom Vieta's formulas:\nSum of roots: α + β = -q/p\n2k + 3k = -q/p\n5k = -q/p  --- (1)\n\nProduct of roots: αβ = r/p\n(2k)(3k) = r/p\n6k² = r/p  --- (2)\n\nFrom (1), k = -q/(5p).\nSubstitute this value of k into (2):\n6 * (-q/(5p))² = r/p\n6 * (q² / (25p²)) = r/p\n6q² / (25p²) = r/p\n\nMultiply both sides by 25p²:\n6q² = (r/p) * 25p²\n6q² = 25pr",
